# owner: a2-release-workflow
#
# Shell scripts are checked out with LF endings on every platform.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout with `core.autocrlf=true` -- the default that
# Git for Windows installs, and what GitHub's windows runner image uses --
# rewrites `.github/scripts/release.sh` to CRLF. `bash` then reads every line as
# ending in a carriage return and passes it on to the command being run, so
# `set -euo pipefail\r` is an unknown option and a quoted path picks up a
# trailing `\r` that no file has in its name.
#
# It matters here rather than only in theory because
# `crates/app/tests/release_workflow.rs` runs those scripts as part of
# `cargo test`, on all three operating systems, and the release workflow's own
# Windows build leg calls them under Git Bash.
*.sh text eol=lf
